From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:02:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] ipa: simple: Lens shading correction

Add an Lsc algorithm: per-channel gain tables on a 17 x 17 grid over the
active area of the sensor, one per colour temperature, from the tuning
file. For each frame the two tables around the AWB colour temperature are
mixed in mireds, weakened in dark scenes (gain' = 1 + s * (gain - 1), s
over the scene light value estimated from exposure time and gain),
resampled on the field of view of the sensor mode (analogue crop), and
handed to the debayer as the lens shading map. The table is rebuilt only
when the colour temperature or the strength changes noticeably.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
